```cs
using Microsoft.VisualStudio.TestTools.UnitTesting;

[TestClass]
public class ArrayListContractTest
{
    [TestMethod]
    public void PUT_InsertContract([FxCopSuppress("Microsoft.Usage", "CA1801:ReviewUnusedParameters")]ArrayList arrList, int x, int index)
    {
        // @@@ last position of x after insertion is less than or equal to original array count 
        Assert.IsTrue(arrList.IndexOf(x) <= index);
    }
}
```
The assertion `Assert.IsTrue(arrList.IndexOf(x) <= index);` in the code above checks whether the last position of `x` after insertion in the `arrList` is less than or equal to the original count. This is based on the assumption that `index` is the position of `x` after the insertion. This assert statement corresponds to the comment "@@@ last position of x after insertion is less than or equal to original array count".

Please note, the actual implementation may vary based on the specific requirements of your code.
